 "notes": [
  "The deposit E_dep is the shower's total hit energy in GeV, summed over its cells, and p its incident momentum: one shower per event.",
  "Each window is the producer's integer momentum bin k, [k, k + 1) GeV, of the shower's own momentum. Per event R = E_est / p; the plotted value is σ/E = s(R)/R̄ in percent (s with ddof = 1), its whisker the 95% χ² interval of s divided by R̄ (N − 1 d.o.f.; R̄'s own uncertainty is neglected, the delta-method se_delta includes it), and its abscissa x = ⟨1/√p⟩ over the window's events. Dividing by p event by event removes the window's own momentum spread and the estimator's bias, and c cancels in s(R)/R̄, so the detector series does not depend on the calibration.",
  "The detector series c·E_dep is a linear-sum benchmark, not a limit: a model that reads the shower's shape (leakage, compensation) can do better than a plain sum.",
  "E on both axes is the incident momentum p as the producer writes it. For a massive species √(p² + m²) differs from p by at most m²/2p², 1.7% for a proton at 5 GeV/c.",
  "σ/E is reported from N = 2; a window is drawn with its whisker from N = 8, and enters the fits and sets the y range from N = 20 and p ≥ 4 GeV.",
  "Fits: a/√E + b and a₀/√E through the origin, by weighted least squares with weights 1/se², se the delta-method standard error of σ/μ recomputed at the fitted value and iterated; χ², ν = n − p and its p-value. Where χ²/ν > 1 the standard errors and the 95% band are scaled by S = √(χ²/ν) (PDG). The band is the 95% confidence band of the line, not the spread of the events. The quadrature form √(a²/E + b²) is fitted as (σ/E)² = A/E + B and tabled, not drawn; its b and the affine b are different constant terms.",
  "Anchors: the lowest bin from 5 GeV, the highest bin and the bin between them nearest in log E to the geometric mean of their centres, chosen on the whole table so they do not move with the selection. A series whose anchor window holds N < 20 takes its nearest window in log E with N ≥ 20 instead; with fewer than two such windows its fit runs through windows of N ≥ 8 and is provisional. The other mode fits every window with N ≥ 20 from 4 GeV.",
  "The top axis is an exact relabelling of the bottom one, E = 1/x²: a deterministic unit conversion, and no data are plotted against it.",
  "Shower: c = Σ p / Σ E_dep = 106 over N = 287 events, fitted once over the whole selection.",
  "The shower is named Electron e⁻: the primary particle of 71 of the 71 selected events with one (100.0%).",
